    "refusal": "101a accepts confirmed native argument-validation refusal as application-refused. Its authenticated same-business-arguments control and stored-state proof remain required. This changed check is in the fresh 79-check set.",
    "runtime": "callAction preserves the existing responseContract/refusalKind enum fields and applicationRejected boolean in its receipt. No new transport, retry, capture, state proof, or acceptance classifier is introduced.",
    "contract": "The Convex application-interface note clarifies native validation before the handler. Existing contract-text equivalence mappings are retained, not broadened by this merge."
  },
